{% from '_macros.j2' import section %}
{{ section(idx, finding, severity_label, repro_curl,
    suggested_title="Backup / source file exposed at " ~ finding.url,
    impact=(
"A backup or pre-deployment artifact is being served by the web tier (`.bak`, `.old`, `.orig`, `.swp`, `~`, `.zip`, "
"`.tar.gz`). Impact tiers: (a) **source-code disclosure** if the file is a server-side script saved as `.bak` — the "
"web server stops interpreting it and returns plaintext source, revealing credentials, business logic, and "
"vulnerabilities for follow-on exploitation; (b) **archive disclosure** if it's a `.zip`/`.tar` of the application — "
"complete code + sometimes `.env` and database dumps; (c) **dev artifact disclosure** (`.swp`, editor temp files) "
"revealing in-progress changes."
),
    validation=(
"1. Confirm the file is the **actual artifact**, not an SPA shell returning 200 HTML. Check `Content-Type` and "
"   the first bytes (`PK\\x03\\x04` for zip, `<?php` for backed-up PHP source, etc.).\n"
"2. If the file is large (multi-MB archive), download a sample (`curl --range 0-65535`) before pulling the whole "
"   thing — confirm the magic bytes match the claimed file type.\n"
"3. Scan the contents for credentials (`grep -r -iE 'password|secret|api_key|aws_'`). Do not test any extracted "
"   credentials.\n"
"4. If the artifact contains source code, identify the most security-relevant files (auth, payments, admin) and "
"   flag specific vulnerabilities found in the source as **additional separate reports**."
),
    note=(
"Submission tactic: lead with the *most sensitive thing the backup contains*, not the backup file URL itself. "
"\"DB credentials for production exposed in source backup\" pays multiples of \"backup file at /index.php.bak\"."
)
) }}
